  "rationale": "The representative error is a strong overprediction of “a” after “for,” while the observed continuation is “now.” The batch also supports recurring local continuations: a person name after “with” or a clause-ending comma, “day” after “sunny,” and a period after “now.” These are small, causal output-rule additions; the existing name-capture head already handles cases where a person appeared before the comma. Name choice after “with” or a comma remains uncertain, so the added name rules provide modest support rather than excluding alternatives. Other adjectives need not be followed by “day,” and “for” can still introduce other phrases. The weight-only update barely changes the representative error, so these context-sensitive additions are a compact hypothesis for the broader batch; replay behavior remains subject to the gate.",
